## alwaysApply: true

You are an expert in **Angular 20**, **TypeScript**, **TailwindCSS**, and **PrimeNG**.  
Apply these coding and theming rules to all project HTML, CSS, and TypeScript files. Prefer separation of concerns: keep design tokens (colors) in `print-theme.mdc` and coding rules here.

## Angular 20 & TypeScript

- Use strict type checking and prefer type inference where appropriate.
- Avoid `any`. Use `unknown` or generics if needed.
- Use standalone components (Angular 20 default). Do not manually set `standalone: true` in decorators.
- Use `signals` for component state and `computed()` for derived values.
- Set `changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush`.
- Use `inject()` for DI; prefer it over constructor injection when possible.
- Use lazy loading for feature routes.
- Keep components small and single-responsibility.
- Use Reactive Forms; avoid template-driven forms.

## Templates & Patterns

- Keep templates simple; avoid heavy logic in templates.
- Use `async` pipe for observables.
- Prefer `[class]` and `[style]` bindings over `ngClass` / `ngStyle`.
- Use native control flow constructs encouraged by Angular v20 where available.

## TailwindCSS rules

- Use Tailwind utilities for layout, spacing, typography (`flex`, `grid`, `gap`, `p-`, `m-`).
- Centralize design tokens in `tailwind.config.js` (colors, spacing, fontSizes).
- Use `@apply` only inside component-specific CSS files; avoid large shared `@apply` clusters.
- Prefer utility composition over creating many custom classes.
- Map CSS variables (from `print-theme.mdc`) to Tailwind config if possible:
  - Keep visual tokens (colors) synchronized with `:root` variables.

## PrimeNG rules

- Use PrimeNG components for complex UI only; wrap them in small presentational components.
- Do not override core PrimeNG styles globally. Use PrimeNG theme variables or `theme.overrides.css`.
- If you must deep-style a PrimeNG component, place overrides in a single dedicated file and scope them (use `::ng-deep` only in that file).
- Prefer applying Tailwind utilities around PrimeNG components for layout and spacing.

## Theming & Colors

- This file **does not** hardcode color values — use CSS variables defined in `print-theme.mdc`.
- Always reference colors as `var(--color-primary)`, `var(--color-cta)`, etc.
- Ensure WCAG contrast for text and interactive elements.

## Additional

- Accessibility: ARIA attributes, keyboard navigation, and focus-visible styles mandatory.
- Code structure: Group by feature, kebab-case filenames, co-locate template/style with component.
